 ("Lift vs own normal level", "How much better the player is under pressure than in his own non-pressure balls, after context adjustment.", "Lift = (pressure RAE or RSE) - (non-pressure RAE or RSE)", "Same as RAE / RSE", "Same eligibility", "The noisiest component (split-half reliability 0.08-0.10). Kept because the problem statement asks for a comparison with usual levels."),
 ("Consistency", "How often the player delivered, match by match.", "Batters: % of pressure innings (>= 6 pressure balls) with runs >= expected runs. Bowlers: % of pressure spells (>= 6 legal pressure balls) with runs conceded <= expected.", "Per player-match aggregates of the above", "Qualifying innings / spells shown per player", "Strongly correlated with output (0.81 batters, 0.84 bowlers)."),
 ("Reliability (shrinkage)", "Discount for small samples.", "Reliability = n / (n + 100), n = pressure balls. Each metric is multiplied by it (consistency is pulled toward the eligible-player average).", "Pressure ball counts", "All eligible players", "k = 100 is a judgement; k = 50 and 200 are tested."),
